/* APEVERSE 2 NEW WORLDS - tokyo_life.js : life in TOKYO (world_tokyo.js builds the city, this runs it).
   - The scramble: a real signal cycle (avenue green -> west road green -> all-way pedestrian scramble), cars that queue at the stop
     lines and wait for you, signal heads that change colour, and a crowd that waits at the four corners and floods across every way
     at once (diagonals included) when the little green man lights up.
   - People: a walking graph over the pavements, Center Gai, the alleys, the yokochō, the shrine and Harajuku; five named residents with
     daily routines and 4-choice conversations that DO things: Haruki (ramen chef), Yumi (DJ), Sora (rhythm-game champion), Mei (shrine
     maiden), Kenta (taxi driver).  Story: "Yumi's test pressing".
   - Businesses (all fictional): ApeMart Express (walk-in konbini), Ramen Kaminari (walk-in, ticket machine -> hand the ticket to the
     chef), Game Center Banana Zone (walk-in: UFO catcher, taiko rhythm drums, purikura), Jazz Kissa Kuroneko (walk-in listening bar),
     Live House SPACE NEKO (walk-in, 19:00-02:00, ticket or guest list, band then DJ, bar, DJ booth), Izakaya Chōchin (walk-in) and the
     yokochō arch bars, Karaoke Utage, Groove Dealers Records, Kaiten Sushi Yūgure, Momo Crêpes, Taiyaki, Sentō Matsu-no-yu, Sakura
     Cycle (rent or buy a bike), ApePhone Store Tokyo, SWAG Tokyo, Harajuku's Takeshita shops, vending machines everywhere.
   - Shrine: offering box, omikuji fortunes, ema wishes, omamori charms, the purification basin.
   - Rides: the Loop Line (elevated train, Shibuya <-> Harajuku, visible all the way), taxis, rental bikes; AI trains run on the viaduct.
   - Festival: Shibuya Bon Odori Matsuri, every Friday 17:00-24:00 on the Apeverse calendar: yagura tower with taiko, lantern rings,
     yatai food stalls, yukata dancers circling the tower from 19:00 (join the circle).  Save: optional S.tokyo. */
